  "description": "The specification's custodial rotation example (lines 1549-1574), keys A0 to A17 written c0 to c17, with its thresholds exactly as the table gives them. The inception and rotation 1 are delivered, with the rotation signed only by the new custodian's c6, c7 and c8. They meet the new signing threshold, but the custodian holds no rotation authority: no signature satisfies the prior next threshold, which only the owner's keys can (lines 1262 and 1574). A validator must not accept the rotation; as a threshold shortfall it should keep it.",
